# Feature Status

Start here to see what each feature does today and what happens next. A blank or unknown item is not complete.

## At a glance

| Feature | Current status | What works now | What remains | Next action | Evidence / detail | Checked |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| No feature recorded yet | unassessed | No behavior verified | Define the first feature | Add its packet and check the current implementation | [Active work items](../work-items/active/README.md) | {{DATE}} |

Use short, user-visible descriptions in the table. Link each feature to its owning packet and the strongest current evidence. Use `unassessed` when the repository has not been checked; do not infer completion from a plan, scaffold, or old report.

Status vocabulary: `unassessed`, `planned`, `in progress`, `partly working`, `verification`, `accepted`, `blocked`. If implementation and documentation disagree, show `needs reconciliation` in the row until they are checked together. Record the verified portion and the unresolved claim separately.

